---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SURFACES = [
  {
    name: 'Landing page',
    badge: 'Active',
    active: true,
    prompt: 'Create a landing page for the AIC product. Audience: operations managers at mid-size manufacturers. Goal: demo requests. Sections: hero with headline and CTA, three benefit cards, closing CTA strip.',
    pushCommand: '/push-to-lab',
  },
  {
    name: 'Presentation',
    badge: 'Coming soon',
    active: false,
    prompt: 'Build a 10-slide pitch deck for a manufacturing prospect. Cover, problem, solution, three product highlights, case study, pricing overview, next steps, thank you.',
    pushCommand: null,
  },
  {
    name: 'Email',
    badge: 'Coming soon',
    active: false,
    prompt: 'Write a re-engagement email for prospects who attended a demo but haven\'t followed up. Warm tone, one clear CTA to book a follow-up call. Under 150 words.',
    pushCommand: null,
  },
  {
    name: 'One-sheet',
    badge: 'Coming soon',
    active: false,
    prompt: 'Create a one-sheet for the iBOM product. Audience: plant managers evaluating digital parts management tools. Lead with the time-saving outcome. One page, print-ready.',
    pushCommand: null,
  },
];
---

<Base title="Generate on-brand" currentPath="/ai-guide/generate">
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">AI guide</p>
    <h1>Generate something new.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Tell the AI what you need and who it's for. Brandforge handles every visual decision automatically — no color names, no font lookups, no brand rules to memorize.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="notice-block">
    <strong>Before you start</strong>
    <p>Open a new session in Claude Code with the Metanoia repo connected. Brandforge loads automatically — you don't need to configure anything. Just start describing what you want to make.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="warning-block">
    <p class="warning-label">Your work lives in the session until you push it</p>
    <p>Anything you generate exists only in your current Claude Code session. If you close the tab or start a new conversation, it's gone. Push your work to its destination before you leave — each surface has its own push command listed below.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="steps-section">
    <h2>How to prompt</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Start a fresh conversation</h3>
          <p>Open a new session each time. A clean slate means Brandforge loads correctly and nothing from a previous session carries over unexpectedly.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Describe what you're making and who it's for</h3>
          <p>Name the asset, the audience, and the goal. Don't describe colors or fonts — describe the communication problem you're solving. Brandforge translates intent into on-brand output.</p>
          <div class="example-prompt">
            <em>"Create a landing page for the AIC product. Audience is operations managers at mid-size manufacturers. Goal is to get them to request a demo. Three sections: hero, key benefits, call to action."</em>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Describe structure, not style</h3>
          <p>Say what sections or pieces you need. Leave every visual decision to Brandforge. If you need to reference something visual, use plain English — the AI will translate it to the right brand value.</p>
          <div class="example-prompt">
            <em>"Hero with a headline, one-sentence subhead, and a button. Three feature cards below. Footer with contact info."</em>
            <span class="example-note">not: "Use the dark navy background with the aqua button."</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Review and direct</h3>
          <p>If something feels off, say so in plain English. "The headline feels too small." "The cards feel cramped." You're directing — Brandforge is executing. You never need to touch the code.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">5</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Push your work</h3>
          <p>When you're happy with the result, use the push command for your surface type. This sends the file to its destination so it exists beyond the session and is accessible to your team.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="surfaces-section">
    <h2>Example prompts by surface</h2>
    <p class="surfaces-intro">Active surfaces can be generated and pushed today. Coming soon surfaces can be previewed in-session but don't have a push command yet — your work will be lost when the session ends.</p>
    <div class="surfaces-list">
      {SURFACES.map(surface => (
        <div class="surface-card">
          <div class="surface-header">
            <span class="surface-name">{surface.name}</span>
            <span class:list={['surface-badge', { 'badge-active': surface.active, 'badge-soon': !surface.active }]}>
              {surface.badge}
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-body">
            <p class="surface-prompt"><em>"{surface.prompt}"</em></p>
            <div class="push-row">
              <span class="push-label">Push command:</span>
              {surface.pushCommand
                ? <code class="push-command">{surface.pushCommand}</code>
                : <span class="push-na">not yet available</span>
              }
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--fs-12);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-36);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
    line-height: var(--lh-tight);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--fs-18);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    max-width: 580px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .notice-block {
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .notice-block strong {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
  }
  .notice-block p {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .warning-block {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--fg-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .warning-label {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--fg-1);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .warning-block p:not(.warning-label) {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
  }

  section { margin-bottom: var(--space-16); }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-24);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-snug);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6); }

  .step { display: flex; gap: var(--space-5); align-items: flex-start; }

  .step-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 32px; height: 32px;
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .step-body h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-16);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .step-body p {
    font-size: var(--fs-15);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .step-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .example-prompt {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .example-note {
    font-size: var(--fs-13);
    color: var(--fg-3);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .surfaces-intro {
    font-size: var(--fs-15);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    max-width: 580px;
  }

  .surfaces-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); }

  .surface-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .surface-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .surface-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-15);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .surface-badge {
    font-size: var(--fs-12);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    padding: 2px var(--space-3);
  }

  .badge-active {
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
  }

  .badge-soon {
    background: var(--bg-muted);
    color: var(--fg-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .surface-body {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .surface-prompt {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .push-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .push-label {
    font-size: var(--fs-13);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--fg-3);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    font-size: var(--fs-12);
  }

  .push-command {
    font-size: var(--fs-13);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    padding: 2px var(--space-2);
  }

  .push-na {
    font-size: var(--fs-13);
    color: var(--fg-3);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
